        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A workshop has \\(45\\) m of black fabric, \\(36\\) m of green fabric, and \\(30\\) m of blue fabric. Each unit of product \\(P\\) requires \\(3\\) m, \\(2\\) m, and \\(1\\) m of these fabrics respectively, while each unit of product \\(Q\\) requires \\(2\\) m, \\(3\\) m, and \\(2\\) m. If the revenue per unit is \\(₹40\\) for \\(P\\) and \\(₹50\\) for \\(Q\\), what is the maximum revenue?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The constraints are \\(3x+2y\\le45\\), \\(2x+3y\\le36\\), \\(x+2y\\le30\\), with \\(x,y\\ge0\\). The first two boundaries intersect at \\(\\left(\\frac{63}{5},\\frac{18}{5}\\right)\\), which also satisfies the blue-fabric constraint. The revenue \\(R=40x+50y\\) is \\(R=40\\cdot\\frac{63}{5}+50\\cdot\\frac{18}{5}=₹684\\).",
